#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-flying.rst:5
#: bb86bd62f6d84d82b10f52121d0d8c91
msgid "Flying a QuadPlane"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-flying.rst:7
#: f68a46b0b31d44c183841e3f2092b81b
msgid "While flying a QuadPlane can actually be easier than flying a conventional fixed wing aircraft there are some things you need to understand. Please read the following sections carefully."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-flying.rst:20
#: e13b0fe258334f06b53625764968d34c
msgid "VTOL vs Fixed-Wing Level Trim"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-flying.rst:22
#: 237828bca640483e932a9f933acf18c0
msgid "Often fixed wing \"level\" trim, which is the pitch attitude stabilization modes attempt to maintain, is set to be several degrees positive with respect to the wing chord line in order to provide lift while cruising. See :ref:`common-accelerometer-calibration` and :ref:`tuning-cruise` for more details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-flying.rst:24
#: a2b2ae3d55694c928090c940708fc8c3
msgid "However, when in VTOL modes, this can result in the vehicle leaning \"backward\" a few degrees, building in a tendency to drift backwards. This can be eliminated by setting the :ref:`Q_TRIM_PITCH<Q_TRIM_PITCH>` parameter to correct this. This can also be used to correct minor CG imbalances caused by VTOL motor placement not being exactly balanced around the CG."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-flying.rst:27
#: 5748c076ccd84111840ec33dd87723b2
msgid "Manual Forward Throttle in VTOL Modes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-flying.rst:29
#: 33b0313327074e9b853ad8f50c686933
msgid "By setting an RC channel option (``RCx_OPTION``) to \"209\", that channel can provide a separate throttle input to the forward motor(s) in QSTABILIZE, QACRO, and QHOVER VTOL modes. This allows forward movement without having to tilt the QuadPlane forward requiring throttle stick repositioning in QSTABILIZE and QACRO to maintain altitude, and present more forward flat plate resistance to forward movement in all modes. The maximum percentage throttle that will be applied by this channel is set by :ref:`Q_FWD_MANTHR_MAX<Q_FWD_MANTHR_MAX>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-flying.rst:34
#: 452c92c71d7a4ce5a0f3beebd2d47c2e
msgid "Radio or Throttle Failsafe"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-flying.rst:36
#: d23858e796d247f0ac9fa597ae4da7a8
msgid "If flying in a plane mode or AUTO, behaviour is determined by the :ref:`FS_SHORT_ACTN<FS_SHORT_ACTN>` and :ref:`FS_LONG_ACTN<FS_LONG_ACTN>` parameter settings (see Plane Failsafe Function). QuadPlanes can be set such that instead of normal plane behaviour on Failsafe induced RTLs, to transition to QRTL and land once at the rally point or home, if  :ref:`Q_RTL_MODE<Q_RTL_MODE>` =1. If :ref:`Q_RTL_MODE<Q_RTL_MODE>` =2, then a fixed wing approach followed by a loiter to alt and QRTL will be executed, similar to that described in the \"AUTO VTOL Landing\" section of :ref:`quadplane-auto-mode`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-flying.rst:38
#: 5c72e08173504ab3ac836b4bc0314a39
msgid "If flying in any VTOL mode (QHOVER,QSTAB,etc.) and not flying a mission, failsafe will evoke QLAND , QRTL or RTL, depending on how :ref:`Q_OPTIONS<Q_OPTIONS>`, bits 5 and 20, are set."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-flying.rst:40
#: 407188a88a064ff29ce515f4b0165775
msgid "if failsafe occurs during a VTOL takeoff, it will immediately switch to QLAND mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-flying.rst:43
#: 92d2b6abb494474cadf823bcb21d8197
msgid "VTOL Landing Repositioning"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-flying.rst:45
#: 71ae31e4956d456b93aae67cff6448b9
msgid "During the final descent phase of QRTL/QLAND or a mission VTOL LAND command, repositioning the vehicle or pausing the descent is usually not possible unless switching to a pilot controlled mode like QLOITER. However, there are two options that can be enabled to give the pilot control:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-flying.rst:48
#: be4a2bfac0d74db886d7584e1c9e38b0
msgid "Throttle Descent Control"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-flying.rst:50
#: 16547ba05b2947c5b997eaef904ca46d
msgid "If :ref:`Q_OPTIONS<Q_OPTIONS>` bit 15(+32768 to param value), is set, it will allow pilot to control descent during VTOL AUTO-LAND phases, similar to throttle stick action during QHOVER or QLOITER. However, this will not become active until the throttle stick is raised above 70% momentarily during the descent at least once."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-flying.rst:53
#: 1d28ee093e844c9c8ff2130ad418a23c
msgid "Horizontal Repositioning"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-flying.rst:55
#: 45c4830765e84fe2b1a90e59ce7bf7d4
msgid "If :ref:`Q_OPTIONS<Q_OPTIONS>` bit 17(+131072 to param value), is set, it will enable pilot horizontal re-positioning during VTOL auto LAND phases using the pitch and roll sticks like QLOITER, momentarily pausing the descent while doing so."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-flying.rst:60
#: 8fc292f06067441db8aa7642c8002bce
msgid "What Will Happen?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-flying.rst:62
#: c43b938d630c429f9f30f8ab14a526fd
msgid "Understanding hybrid aircraft can be difficult at first, so below are some scenarios and how the ArduPilot code will handle them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-flying.rst:66
#: 67f0dc7f3f294c088224004e934cc10b
msgid "I am hovering in QHOVER/QLOITER and switch to FBWA mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-flying.rst:68
#: c12035455a884381a98ba5762c324f10
msgid "The aircraft will continue to hover, setting forward thrust/throttle at whatever the throttle stick position dictates and gaining speed. If you zero throttle during the transition, the aircraft will continue to hold the current height and hold itself level, slowing to a halt. It will drift with the wind as it is not doing position hold."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-flying.rst:71
#: ead57c57b409486698e48f6564bc658c
msgid "If you advance the throttle stick then the forward motor will throttle-up and the aircraft will start to move forward. The quad motors will continue to provide both lift and stability while the aircraft is moving slowly. You can control the attitude of the aircraft with roll and pitch stick input. When you use the pitch stick (elevator) that will affect the climb rate of the quad motors. If you pull back on the elevator the quad motors will assist with the aircraft climb. If you push forward on the pitch stick the power to the quad motors will decrease and the aircraft will descend."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-flying.rst:81
#: 9ef64d594c2f4b6eb7ee0849c24291a9
msgid "The roll and pitch input also controls the attitude of the aircraft, so a right roll at low speed will cause the aircraft to move to the right. It will also cause the aircraft to yaw to the right (as the QuadPlane code interprets right aileron in fixed wing mode as a commanded turn)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-flying.rst:86
#: 22fbbaddb90241a49469b72fdad9c37e
msgid "Once the aircraft reaches an airspeed of :ref:`AIRSPEED_MIN <AIRSPEED_MIN>` (or :ref:`Q_ASSIST_SPEED <Q_ASSIST_SPEED>` if that is set and is greater than :ref:`AIRSPEED_MIN <AIRSPEED_MIN>`) the amount of assistance the quad motors provide will decrease over 5 seconds. After that time the aircraft will be flying purely as a fixed wing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-flying.rst:92
#: 32a96d08a4e24dada7a9f8c187559d80
msgid "I am flying fast in FBWA mode and switch to QHOVER mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-flying.rst:94
#: bcd9c69b30d94c6d984cb588c117b6e1
msgid "The quad motors will immediately engage and will start by holding the aircraft at the current height. The climb/descent rate is now set by the throttle stick, with a higher throttle stick meaning climb and a lower throttle stick meaning descend. At mid-stick the aircraft will hold altitude."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-flying.rst:100
#: 9d5493f50792451e94b0d36c2136fa04
msgid "The forward motor will stop, but the aircraft will continue to move forward due to its momentum. The drag of the air will slowly bring it to a stop. The attitude of the aircraft can be controlled with roll and pitch sticks (aileron and elevator). You can yaw the aircraft with rudder."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-flying.rst:107
#: 1e21953fe8534640a3c6902587715340
msgid "I switch to RTL mode while hovering"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-flying.rst:109
#: 768c7c6e22544aeab97a4788dac8e92d
msgid "The aircraft will generally transition to fixed wing flight. The quad motors will provide assistance with lift and attitude while the forward motor starts to pull the aircraft forward. Depending on the :ref:`Q_RTL_MODE<Q_RTL_MODE>`, different behaviors can be selected as it returns to the return point (rally or home). See :ref:`quadplane_rtl` for details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-flying.rst:115
#: 93b68de946584ea19832dd0a7b53f8e6
msgid "If you have :ref:`RTL_AUTOLAND <RTL_AUTOLAND>` setup then the aircraft will follow the mission configuration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-flying.rst:120
#: 9e9b884aa6844963b300bc03720909d4
msgid "I switch into QRTL close to HOME"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-flying.rst:122
#: 66d8e01d89be4d5484da2c3eac1fa548
msgid "If closer than 1.5X the larger of either :ref:`RTL_RADIUS<RTL_RADIUS>` or :ref:`WP_LOITER_RAD<RTL_RADIUS>`, then the vehicle will proceed toward home in VTOL mode and land. If greater, it will transition to fixed wing, climbing toward :ref:`RTL_ALTITUDE<RTL_ALTITUDE>` and executing a normal QRTL. Depending on how far from home, the vehicle may only briefly climb and then switch back to approach or airbrake phases. The further away, the higher the climb as it flies back toward home. If the approach behavior has ben disabled with :ref:`Q_OPTIONS<Q_OPTIONS>` bit 16, then it will just switch to VTOL (if not already in that mode, navigate to home and land)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-flying.rst:125
#: b9e2615670fa40a78e70cac4759a1e36
msgid "I have an EKF Failsafe"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-flying.rst:127
#: 077a7509219445a9b444695e58233f1a
msgid "ArduPilot provides a failsafe mechanism to protect VTOL operation in case the EKF becomes unhealthy. In normal fixed wing operation, ArduPilot \"falls back\" to another inertial guidance filter, DCM, if the EKF becomes unhealthy. However, if operating in AUTO mode in a VTOL mode when an EKF failure occurs, QuadPlanes will switch modes to QLAND, and to QHOVER in all other position control VTOL modes (QLOITER, QRTL, QLAND, QAUTOTUNE)."
msgstr ""

